info:
  program: nails
  args:
    - config
    - "--help"
---
success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Inspect and check the configuration file (nails.toml)

Usage: nails config [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  path      Print the resolved configuration file path and whether it exists
  show      Print the effective configuration and where each value comes from
  validate  Check a configuration file strictly (syntax, types, unknown keys)
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -c, --config <PATH>
          Path to the configuration file (overrides binary-relative discovery)

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostics on stderr: -v for debug, -vv for trace

  -q, --quiet
          Print only errors and the final result

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use colour

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a stream only when it is a terminal, TERM is not `dumb` and NO_COLOR is unset or empty
          - always: Always colour, even when piped
          - never:  Never colour

          [default: auto]

      --ascii
          Use ASCII markers instead of Unicode symbols and box drawing

      --json
          Print machine-readable JSON on stdout

      --no-log-file
          Do not write the log file on the hidden volume (diagnostics still go to stderr)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

----- stderr -----
